# Task 1: analytics run history — `version` becomes optional on the store read

## Context

Analytics run history is moving off the Knowledge Graph → Analytics tab and
onto the Knowledge Graph → Management → Runs page, as a second table below
the existing build-runs table. That page has no version filter, so the read
needs to span every version of a domain in one call. This is the bottom of
that stack: `load_graph_analytics_runs` gains an optional `version`, and
`version=None` returns the whole folder's history, newest-first, instead of
one version's.

## Changes

1. `src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py` — `load_graph_analytics_runs`
   contract widened to `version: Optional[str] = None`; docstring documents
   that `None` spans every version.
2. `src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py` — Same signature
   change. The `WHERE` clause only appends `AND r.version = %s` when
   `version is not None`; the `ORDER BY r.computed_at DESC, r.id DESC` was
   already correct for the multi-version case and is unchanged.
3. `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py` — Pass-through wrapper's
   signature widened the same way; docstring/error handling unchanged.
4. `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py` — `_InMemoryStore` fake's
   `_graph_analytics_runs` map now stores `(seq, row)` tuples (a monotonic
   counter standing in for `computed_at`, since the fake has no real
   timestamp to order cross-version reads by) instead of plain dicts;
   `record_graph_analytics_run` tags each row with the version it was
   recorded under (`row.setdefault("version", version)`) and
   `load_graph_analytics_runs` filters by folder (and by version only when
   given), then sorts by sequence descending. Added four new tests: a read
   with no version spans all versions newest-first, each returned row
   carries its `version`, `limit` applies across the merged version set,
   and other folders are excluded. The four pre-existing
   `graph_analytics_runs` tests (empty-by-default, newest-first, limit,
   scoped-by-version) still pass unchanged, so explicit-version scoping is
   still fully supported.

## Modified Files

- `src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py`
- `src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py`
- `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py`
- `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`

