```bash
env -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE \
    -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET -u LAKEBASE_PROJECT \
    -u LAKEBASE_BRANCH -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE \
    -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE_RESOURCE_SEGMENT -u LAKEBASE_SCHEMA \
    .venv/bin/pytest -q -m "not scenario"
```

`3772 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected, 1 xfailed, 0 failed` (registry
subset: `332 passed`). Only one existing call site
(`src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py:719`), not the three the task brief
assumed — it passes `version` positionally and is unaffected either way.

Note: because the `_InMemoryStore` fake fully overrides the abstract method,
the four new fake-based tests passed as soon as the fake was updated (before
`base.py`/`store.py`/`RegistryService.py` were touched), rather than failing
with the `TypeError` the brief predicted. See
`.superpowers/sdd/task-1-report.md` for the full account.

# Fix pass 1: code review remediation for commit cb4bddd

## Context

A code review of `cb4bddd` (the task above) raised two Important findings:
the production Lakebase SQL branch for `load_graph_analytics_runs` had no
test coverage of its own (only the `_InMemoryStore` fake was exercised), and
`RegistryService.load_graph_analytics_runs`'s docstring still described the
old version-scoped-only contract. Both are fixed; no production behaviour
changed.

## Changes

1. `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py` — Added
   `TestLakebaseGraphAnalyticsRunsSql`, driving the real
   `LakebaseRegistryStore.load_graph_analytics_runs` via the existing
   scripted-cursor harness (`_make_lakebase_store` + `_ScriptedCursor` +
   `_ScriptedConn`, following the `_collab_store` pattern — table-ready flag
   short-circuited via `_graph_analytics_runs_ready = True`). Two tests
   assert on the captured `(sql, params)` tuple: `version=None` emits SQL
   without `r.version = %s` and params `("rid-1", "demo", 50)`; `version="1"`
   emits SQL with the predicate and params `("rid-1", "demo", "1", 50)`,
   checked as an exact ordered tuple so a future reordering of the
   `.append()` calls would be caught. Verified this by temporarily swapping
   the append order in `store.py` (limit appended before the version
   predicate) — the new `version="1"` test failed as expected — then
   reverted the swap (confirmed via `git diff` showing no residual change).
2. `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py` — Rewrote the
   `load_graph_analytics_runs` docstring from "Newest-first analytics run
   history for *folder*/*version*." (wrong once `version` is optional) to
   state it spans every version unless `version` scopes it.

## Modified Files

- `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`
- `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py`

## Test Result

```bash
env -u DATABRICKS_HOST -u DATABRICKS_TOKEN -u DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE \
    -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID -u DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET -u LAKEBASE_PROJECT \
    -u LAKEBASE_BRANCH -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE \
    -u LAKEBASE_DATABASE_RESOURCE_SEGMENT -u LAKEBASE_SCHEMA \
    .venv/bin/pytest -q -m "not scenario"
```

`3774 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected, 1 xfailed, 0 failed` (full suite);
`tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`: `72 passed`.
